ing margins are contracting by -3.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $209M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.0pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 131% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3066130201558854},{"text":"SGA costs surged 226% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (71% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.286},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 63/100): durably derated by the market; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","c